{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"=== STATUS UPDATE: J11's SUITE IS BUILT AND LANDED. WHAT REMAINS IS FOUR PRODUCT BUGS IT FOUND. ===\n\nWHERE THE CELLS STAND. Harness run 30731818113 (main @ 338e397335): **43 passed / 6 failed**, up\nfrom 29/19 two runs earlier. Everything this story owed structurally is now on main:\n  * the 28-cell mutation table (`test_dc_mutations.py`), per-mutation idempotence as its OWN cell,\n    the positive identity assertion, and the config file-content isolation check;\n  * PAGINATION PASSES with real measurements — server-echoed maxResults=1000, reconciler page_size\n    100, 201 issues seeded to force three pages, **201 of 201 recovered**. That is live evidence\n    against the truncation class that shipped three times in this epic (1105, 9263, deac);\n  * the canary hole I introduced is closed (change 1203, merged as df41edcf2): moving the helpers\n    into `_dc_support` had removed `_live_jira_ready` from two modules, so the 22-cell table and\n    the store-copy slice were invisible to the all-skip canary. Measured: collected=0 before,\n    collected=29 after.\n\n**THE SIX REMAINING FAILURES ARE NOT THIS STORY'S TEST DEFECTS. Four are product bugs with their\nown tickets, and that is the correct decomposition — do not \"fix\" them here.**\n  * [rebar:727f-b351-59ba-4b3b] phantom outbound update (the idempotence cell) — root cause proven,\n    fix written, BLOCKED on a live disagreement; see that ticket.\n  * [rebar:d103-c3f8-2fbc-4c97] snapshot-absent key planned as an outbound create (the inbound-probe\n    cell).\n  * inbound link not surfacing as a local dep — still unowned, needs root-causing.\n  * outbound transition-status — [rebar:7f93-2743-a597-4f98] fixed the INBOUND half (that cell now\n    passes, and reached its oracle for the first time), but the outbound half still fails. Needs\n    its own diagnosis; do not assume 7f93 covers it.\n  * the inbound-assignee cell is MY TEST'S FAULT, already triaged: local tickets store assignee as\n    a bare string on BOTH deployments by design, and this story's own plan said the identity is not\n    a field on the ticket JSON. The oracle must assert the PASS minted the identity, not compare\n    `ensure_identity_for`'s return against itself (which can never fail).\n  * inbound edit-summary is FIXED by [rebar:b9b8-1c40-ea53-4ef3] (merged ae009443a9) and should be\n    green on the next run.\n\nSO THE CLOSE PATH IS: land 727f + d103, root-cause the inbound-link and outbound-transition cells,\nfix the assignee oracle, re-run the harness, and close on a green suite. This story does NOT close\nwhile cells are red — its ACs require each mutation asserted individually."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785687875650899001,"uuid":"119dd4cf-fcc6-48c2-a3e2-c679294b8720"}